{"version": 2, "width": 80, "height": 42, "title": "help", "env": {"TERM": "xterm-256color", "SHELL": "/bin/sh"}}
[0.103367, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;34mUsage:\u001b[0m   \r\n  /home/damian/opensource/remote/projects/resolver/worktrees/pip-without-rich-20261026/.nox/test-3-14/bin/python -m pip <command> [options]\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;34mCommands:\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36minstall                    \u001b[0m Install packages.\r\n  \u001b[36mlock                       \u001b[0m Generate a lock file.\r\n  \u001b[36mdownload                   \u001b[0m Download packages.\r\n  \u001b[36muninstall                  \u001b[0m Uninstall packages.\r\n  \u001b[36mfreeze                     \u001b[0m Output installed packages in requirements format.\r\n  \u001b[36minspect                    \u001b[0m Inspect the python environment.\r\n  \u001b[36mlist                       \u001b[0m List installed packages.\r\n  \u001b[36mshow                       \u001b[0m Show information about installed packages.\r\n  \u001b[36mcheck                      \u001b[0m Verify installed packages have compatible dependencies.\r\n  \u001b[36mconfig                     \u001b[0m Manage local and global configuration.\r\n  \u001b[36msearch                     \u001b[0m Search PyPI for packages.\r\n  \u001b[36mcache                      \u001b[0m Inspect and manage pip's wheel cache.\r\n  \u001b[36mindex                      \u001b[0m Inspect information available from package indexes.\r\n  \u001b[36mwheel                      \u001b[0m Build wheels from your requirements.\r\n  \u001b[36mhash                       \u001b[0m Compute hashes of package archives.\r\n  \u001b[36mcompletion                 \u001b[0m A helper command used for command completion.\r\n  \u001b[36mdebug                      \u001b[0m Show information useful for debugging.\r\n  \u001b[36mhelp                       \u001b[0m Show help for commands.\r\n\r\n \u001b[32m-V\u001b[0m, \u001b[36m--version\u001b[0m                Show version and exit.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;34mGeneral Options:\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[32m-h\u001b[0m, \u001b[36m--help\u001b[0m                  Show help.\r\n  \u001b[36m--debug\u001b[0m                     Let unhandled exceptions propagate outside the\r\n                              main subroutine, instead of logging them to\r\n                              stderr.\r\n  \u001b[36m--isolated\u001b[0m                  Run pip in an isolated mode, ignoring\r\n                              environment variables and user configuration.\r\n  \u001b[36m--require-virtualenv\u001b[0m        Allow pip to only run in a virtual environment;\r\n                              exit with an error otherwise.\r\n  \u001b[36m--python\u001b[0m \u001b[33m<python>\u001b[0m           Run pip with the specified Python interpreter.\r\n  \u001b[32m-v\u001b[0m, \u001b[36m--verbose\u001b[0m               Give more output. Option is additive, and can be\r\n                              used up to 3 times.\r\n  \u001b[32m-q\u001b[0m, \u001b[36m--quiet\u001b[0m                 Give less output. Option is additive, and can be\r\n                              used up to 3 times (corresponding to WARNING,\r\n                              ERROR, and CRITICAL logging levels).\r\n  \u001b[36m--log\u001b[0m \u001b[33m<path>\u001b[0m                Path to a verbose appending log.\r\n  \u001b[36m--no-input\u001b[0m                  Disable prompting for input.\r\n  \u001b[36m--keyring-provider\u001b[0m \u001b[33m<keyring_provider>\u001b[0m\r\n                              Enable the credential lookup via the keyring\r\n                              library if user input is allowed. Specify which\r\n                              mechanism to use [auto, disabled, import,\r\n                              subprocess]. (default: auto)\r\n  \u001b[36m--proxy\u001b[0m \u001b[33m<proxy>\u001b[0m             Specify a proxy in the form\r\n                              scheme://[user:passwd@]proxy.server:port.\r\n  \u001b[36m--no-proxy-env\u001b[0m              Do not read proxy configuration from environment\r\n                              variables.\r\n  \u001b[36m--retries\u001b[0m \u001b[33m<retries>\u001b[0m         Maximum attempts to establish a new HTTP\r\n                              connection. (default: 5)\r\n  \u001b[36m--timeout\u001b[0m \u001b[33m<sec>\u001b[0m             Set the socket timeout (default 15 seconds).\r\n  \u001b[36m--exists-action\u001b[0m \u001b[33m<action>\u001b[0m    Default action when a path already exists:\r\n                              (s)witch, (i)gnore, (w)ipe, (b)ackup, (a)bort.\r\n  \u001b[36m--trusted-host\u001b[0m \u001b[33m<hostname>\u001b[0m   Mark this host or host:port pair as trusted,\r\n                              even though it does not have valid or any HTTPS.\r\n  \u001b[36m--cert\u001b[0m \u001b[33m<path>\u001b[0m               Path to PEM-encoded CA certificate bundle. If\r\n                              provided, overrides the default. See 'SSL\r\n                              Certificate Verification' in pip documentation\r\n                              for more information.\r\n  \u001b[36m--client-cert\u001b[0m \u001b[33m<path>\u001b[0m        Path to SSL client certificate, a single file\r\n                              containing the private key and the certificate\r\n                              in PEM format.\r\n  \u001b[36m--cache-dir\u001b[0m \u001b[33m<dir>\u001b[0m           Store the cache data in <dir>.\r\n  \u001b[36m--no-cache-dir\u001b[0m              Disable the cache.\r\n  \u001b[36m--disable-pip-version-check\u001b[0m\r\n                              Don't periodically check PyPI to determine\r\n                              whether a new version of pip is available for\r\n                              download. Implied with\u001b[36m --no-\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m                              index\u001b[0m.\r\n  \u001b[36m--no-color\u001b[0m                  Suppress colored output.\r\n  \u001b[36m--use-feature\u001b[0m \u001b[33m<feature>\u001b[0m     Enable new functionality, that may be backward\r\n                              incompatible.\r\n  \u001b[36m--use-deprecated\u001b[0m \u001b[33m<feature>\u001b[0m  Enable deprecated functionality, that will be\r\n                              removed in the future.\r\n  \u001b[36m--resume-retries\u001b[0m \u001b[33m<resume_retries>\u001b[0m\r\n                              Maximum attempts to resume or restart an\r\n                              incomplete download. (default: 5)\r\n"]
